SUMMARY:Upstairs at Helium: Daniel Simonsen
LOCATION:Portland
DESCRIPTION:Originally from Norway\, Daniel Simonsen is a Norwegian/Chilean
  stand-up comedian. He can be seen in Stavros Halkias’s feature\, Let’s
  Start A Cult on Hulu and Joe Pera's new Adult Swim series\, My Two Cars. D
 aniel regularly opens for Louis CK and has also opened for Stavros Halkias\
 , Bert Kreischer\, Ari Shaffir\, and performed at Dave Chappelle’s YS Fir
 ehouse. He made his US late-night debut on Late Night with Seth Meyers. He 
 has since appeared on CC Stand-Up Featuring\, The Late Show with Stephen Co
 lbert\, Stavvy’s World\, and recurred on Comedy Central’s This Week at 
 the Comedy Cellar. Daniel’s Colbert performance was reviewed by Vulture. 
 He was named NY's Funniest at the NYCF and performs at the Edinburgh Fringe
  Festival regularly. He won UK’s So You Think You’re Funny award and we
 nt on to win the Best Newcomer award after that.\n\nWhile in the UK\, Danie
 l had a recurring role on Vic and Bob’s BBC sitcom\, House of Fools and I
 TV’s Timewasters. He created and wrote his own digital series for ALL4 ca
 lled\, Daniel directed by Andrew Gaynord (People of the Earth\, Netflix Pre
 sents: The Characters\, Detroiters\, Stath Lets Flats\, etc.) that starred 
 him\, Natasia Demetriou\, and Brett Goldstein. He also appeared on Russell 
 Howard’s Good News. He is a Comedy Cellar regular and tours nationwide an
 d internationally.\n\nCouples Package includes:\n\n- 2 premium seats\n- $90
  food & beverage credit ($45 per person)\n- Gratuity\n- Ticket Protection\n
 \n**The Private Skybox Suite includes up to 10 tickets\, a $400 Food & Beve
 rage voucher\, a personal server\, a private restroom\, and all gratuity ch
 arges.\n\nAny additional food and drink costs above $400 will be billed at 
 the end of the show. The guest count can not exceed 10 people. All club pol
 icies and safety guidelines will be enforced. Please note that the skybox i
 s on the second floor of our showroom\, and is NOT wheelchair accessible.\n
 More info: https://comedyatlas.app/comedy-atlas/event/upstairs-at-helium-da
